    - For each of the 3 colors, independently pick a rot_k in {0,1,2,3} at random; require at least one rot_k > 0 so at least one cue exists
    - For each color with rot_k > 0, compute cue_size in {1..5} with cue_size % 4 == (-rot_k) % 4 (i.e. size satisfies size mod 4 = 4-rot_k mod 4)
    - Build the INPUT by rotating the output c-layer mask by rot_k quarter turns CCW (equivalent to np.rot90(mask, rot_k)) for each color -> this inverts the solver's CW rotation
    - Place the (input) NxN board at a random position in the 20x20 grid leaving a peripheral bg band of >= 5 cells on at least one side
    - For each rotating color, generate a monochromatic cue sprite of size=cue_size (random 8-connected blob) and place it in the bg region such that its bbox Chebyshev distance to the board bbox is >= 4 and to other cues is >= 2
    - Verify: (a) board bbox is largest connected component; (b) no cue component lies within margin-3 of the board bbox; (c) running the solver on the generated input reproduces the constructed output
